 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h2><p>Inf=
erence efficiency remains one of the most important practical topics for LL=
Ms. For example, more efficient inference saves big LLM providers tons of m=
oney, lets individual users run larger models faster on consumer hardware, =
and is especially important in long-context (e.g., agent) use cases.</p><p>=
The papers below cover KV-cache reuse, pruning, efficient attention kernels=
, decoding methods, and memory-aware serving.</p><p><span>Here, I would pic=
k </span><em><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.05451">FlashAttention-4:=
 Algorithm and Kernel Pipelining Co-Design for Asymmetric Hardware Scaling<=
/a></em><span>, which is the successor of the popular FlashAttention 1-3 im=
plementations.</span></p><p>Side note: FlashAttention is an implementation-=
level improvement that computes the same attention result as standard atten=
tion. The trick is that it reorganizes the computation to avoid slow memory=
 movement and use the GPU more efficiently. However, mathematically, the mo=
del still uses the same attention operation, so the output should be equiva=
lent up to small numerical differences from floating-point arithmetic.</p><=
p>Back to the paper: FlashAttention-4 is interesting because attention is s=
till one of the core bottlenecks for long-context LLMs, and FlashAttention-=
style kernels have a wide-ranging effect through downstream libraries. Simi=
lar to FlashAttention 1 to 3, I expect FlashAttention 4 to be widely used i=
nside all kinds of libraries, from PyTorch and Hugging Face transformers to=
 vLLM, SGLang, and other high-throughput serving stacks.</p><p>So, what=E2=
=80=99s new in FlashAttention-4? The main point of the paper is that the mo=
re recent Blackwell GPUs changed the bottleneck. On B200 and GB200, tensor =
core throughput increased a lot compared to other parts of the chip. (Share=
d memory bandwidth and exponential units become relatively more limiting.) =
So, attention kernels now need to use tensor cores well while keeping the n=
on-matrix-multiplication parts from slowing down the whole kernel.</p><p>Fl=
ashAttention-4 addresses this with a set of kernel and algorithm changes. F=
or example, the paper describes several low-level GPU optimizations, includ=
ing larger computation blocks, asynchronous matrix multiplications, faster =
approximate exponentials for softmax, better memory usage, and a backward p=
ass that splits work across two cooperating CUDA thread blocks.</p><div cla=
