ce there are lots of interesting subcategories to discuss.)</p><p><span>One=
 interesting paper here is </span><em><a href=3D"https://arxiv.org/abs/2605=
.15184">Is Grep All You Need? How Agent Harnesses Reshape Agentic Search</a=
></em><span>. I like this paper because it studies a very practical questio=
n that comes up all the time when building agents / agent harnesses. Should=
 an agent use fancy vector search (think RAG) in semantic space, or can sim=
ple lexical search such as </span><code>grep</code><span> be enough?</span>=
</p><p><span>The paper compares grep-style lexical search and vector search=
