<p>I hope you found this list useful as a personal reference, and it gives =
you a glimpse into the recent developments on the research front.</p><p>Loo=
king across the papers, there is still plenty of work on larger and stronge=
r models. Also, a lot of the interesting progress is now about using comput=
e more selectively (sparse attention, KV-cache improvements, faster attenti=
on kernels, more targeted data pipelines, training methods that try to get =
more out of the same model).</p><p>Another recurring theme is that model qu=
ality increasingly depends on the surrounding system (agent harnesses, tool=
-use data, inference-time sampling). That makes the boundary between =E2=80=
=9Cmodel research=E2=80=9D and =E2=80=9Csystems research=E2=80=9D blurrier =
than it used to be.</p><p><strong>Thanks for reading and for supporting Ahe=
ad of AI. These curated lists take time to maintain, but I find them useful=
